# Client .deb after UI changes

If the change touches the desktop shell UI, build a new `.deb` in the same turn. Do not wait for the user to ask.

Counts as UI: `client/web/src/**`, `client/web/e2e/**`, `client/artek_buddy.py`, `client/url`, `client/VERSION`.

```bash
client/build-deb.sh
```

- Writes `artek-buddy-client_<VERSION>_all.deb` in the repo root. Gitignored. Do not commit it.
- Bump `VERSION` / `client/VERSION` first if this is a new ship. Never overwrite an already shipped filename (e.g. leave `…_0.9.2_all.deb` and write `…_0.9.3_all.deb`).
- Host-only changes (API, memory, runtime, compose) do not need a new `.deb`.
- After building, tell the user the filename so they can `dpkg -i` it on the desktop PC.
